# RescueGrid System Rules & Memory Guard

- User Roles:
  - DONOR (Food Producer): Posts surplus, verifies arriving driver OTPs, views ESG metrics.
  - SHELTER (Food Consumer): Scans radar, claims batches (full/partial), gets 6-digit OTP pass, confirms delivery.
- Atomic Concurrency:
  - Redis Lua script enforces single-winner atomic locking.
  - 3-Tier priority windows (0-5m Tier 1 exclusive, 5-15m Tier 2 top-5, >15m open).
- Biological Countdown:
  - Never reset expiration timers on cancellation.
  - If cancelled with >15m left, restore to radar with remaining TTL.
  - If cancelled with <=15m left, transition to EXPIRED.
- Cryptographic OTP:
  - 6-digit HMAC-SHA256 code verified with crypto.timingSafeEqual. Rate-limited to 5 failed attempts per 5 minutes.
- Rule: Do not modify working code unless explicitly requested by the user.
